# ---- Section 8 ----
para("| 1 | Similar-submission retrieval quality |", "| 1 | Similar-submission retrieval quality | nDCG@10 on a test set ordered by submission date (50 test queries per data track), graded by judges on a four-level scale; paired comparison of the hybrid configuration with a BM25 baseline (paired bootstrap interval; randomization test reported beside it) | Mean paired difference reported with its 95% interval. \"Not worse than BM25 by more than 0.05\" is stated only if the lower bound of the interval lies above −0.05, \"better\" only if it lies above 0; otherwise the result is reported as inconclusive. At or above an absolute floor fixed after the pilot. Being better than BM25 is not required |")
para("| 2 | Solution-example relevance |", "| 2 | Solution-example relevance | Share of the first five examples shown that address at least part of the need (P@5), on 40 test need statements per registered source, with the source type stated; rate of wrongly reporting \"no example found\", measured against the judged pool (a lower bound) and checked at greater depth on a sample of queries | P@5: same comparison, interval rule and floor as specification 1, margin 0.05. \"No example found\" error rate: reported as a lower bound with an exact interval; no target |")
para("| 3 | External prior-art relevance |", "| 3 | External prior-art relevance | Share of need statements with at least one relevant patent in the top 10 (success@10), for automatic queries edited at the approval step (by a project judge in the assessor role, or a sponsor assessor if available) compared with unaided keyword queries, on 30 judged need statements | Paired difference reported with its 95% interval as an estimate. No non-inferiority or superiority claim is made: 30 statements are too few to support one |")
para("| 7 | Response time |", "| 7 | Response time | 95th-percentile time from opening a submission to display of the similar-submission and solution-example results, at corpus sizes of 10,000 and 100,000 items, on the reference environment | ≤ 5 s (planning value, to be confirmed) |")
para("The margins of 0.05 and 0.10,", "The margin of 0.05, the response-time value, the corpus sizes and the test-set sizes are planning values that await owner confirmation before the evaluation protocol is frozen. Retrieval targets are stated relative to a lexical baseline because no defensible absolute value exists before evaluation. The test sets are sized for a six-month project with project judges, so the intervals may be wide: a comparison whose interval does not clear the stated bound is reported as inconclusive, never as equivalence (Section 12, activity 2). Test-set sizes are per task and data track. Every result will be reported with the data behind it: sponsor data, or substitute data labelled as such.")

# ---- Section 12: problem-solving logic ----
para("Where a solution-example source can be imported as a collection,", "Where a solution-example source can be imported as a collection, finding similar submissions and finding solution examples are the same retrieval problem applied to different collections; a source reachable only through an external service is connected through the connector contract of activity 4 instead. One retrieval service therefore ranks every imported collection, and each collection has its own lexical and vector index. Identical and near-identical submissions are flagged by content hashes and word-shingle fingerprints before ranking. The ranking configuration set is kept deliberately small: BM25 as the lexical baseline, one multilingual dense encoder used without fine-tuning, and the combination of the two by reciprocal rank fusion, which is fixed in advance as the primary configuration. No single method leads across public benchmarks (Thakur et al., 2021; Muennighoff et al., 2023) and no benchmark of need or challenge submissions was found (Section 6), so the evaluation asks one practical question: whether adding semantic retrieval to BM25 helps on this kind of text enough to justify its cost.")
para("Every retrieval result belongs to one of two data tracks", "Every retrieval result belongs to one of two data tracks that are never pooled. The sponsor-data track runs only if the sponsor releases data, and is judged by sponsor assessors where they can take part. The substitute-data track uses public or constructed collections and project judges. Test sets are split by submission date. BM25 uses the toolkit's default parameters and reciprocal rank fusion the constant of its original publication, so no ranking parameter is tuned; display thresholds are set on an earlier development segment, and each configuration is run once on the later test segment after the protocol has been frozen. A comparison is reported as better, not worse by more than the margin, inconclusive, worse, or below floor. The prototype is not required to be better than the BM25 baseline.")
drop("| all-MiniLM-L6-v2 |")
