# ---- activity 6 ----
para("The outputs of activities 3 to 5 are integrated", "The outputs of activities 3 to 5 are integrated into one release, built from tagged sources by deployment scripts on a clean instance of the reference environment; the release is accepted when all their test suites pass on it. Pilot judging follows on the ten development queries per task. It measures agreement between judges, using Krippendorff's alpha on the ordinal scale (Hayes and Krippendorff, 2007) and Cohen's kappa on the binary split (Cohen, 1960), and the time per judgment. It allows one revision of the judging guide, and the graded scales for similar submissions and solution examples are collapsed to three levels if alpha stays below 0.67 after the revision; 0.67 is a planning value set by the project. The planned test sets are 50 queries for similar submissions, 40 need statements per solution-example source and 30 need statements for external prior art, sized for the judging time of a six-month project, not for a target statistical power. Error rates in retrieval comparisons depend on the number of topics and on the size of the observed difference (Voorhees and Buckley, 2002); the pilot standard deviation of per-query differences therefore gives the expected width of each interval at the planned size, and the protocol records before the test run whether a statement against the margin is likely to be reachable. If it is not, the report says so in advance and presents the comparison as an estimate. Absolute floors are fixed and dated before the test run.")
para("The retrieval configuration is selected on the development split only", "The primary configuration is fixed in the protocol, so development data are used only for thresholds and the pilot. Test pools are judged blind to configuration, with 20% of query-item pairs judged by two judges and disagreements adjudicated by a third. For five randomly sampled test queries per task and track whose judged pool contains no relevant item, items ranked 11 to 30 by any configuration are also judged. The test split is run once per configuration, and the approval, re-approval, disclosure, attribution and response-time tests are run on the release.")
para("The evaluation report states every result", "The evaluation report states every result with its data track, confidence interval and outcome label, never combines sponsor-data and substitute-data results, and reports a secondary comparison whose interval includes zero as \"no supported difference\". It reports the \"no example found\" error rate as a lower bound measured against the judged pool, beside the estimate from the deeper check. If on a track the hybrid configuration is not shown to be not worse than BM25 by more than the margin, or falls below its floor, the report says so and the as-built specification makes BM25 the default configuration for that kind of collection. Because relevance judgments vary between judges (Voorhees, 2000), the comparisons are repeated with each judge's own grades on the double-judged subset to check whether the direction of each result is stable. An error analysis classifies the hybrid configuration's failures on the test queries, for example vocabulary mismatch, long or multi-topic text and language, and directs corrective development before handover; corrected code is described in the report and is not re-scored on the test split. Judging and sample-size risks are listed in Section 17 (risks 10 and 12). If sponsor assessors can take part, a structured walk-through of the review screens records how they use them; the evaluation does not depend on it.")

# ---- activity 7 ----
sub("The instructions are accepted when a person not involved in the build deploys the release from them and the rehearsal is recorded; who that person is will be decided with the team composition.", "The instructions are accepted when a team member who did not write the deployment scripts deploys the release from them on a clean instance and the rehearsal is recorded. A final reproducibility check recomputes every reported figure from the stored run and judgment files.")

# ---- limits ----
para("The evaluation measures retrieval quality on judged test sets", "The evaluation measures retrieval quality on judged test sets and the conformance of the workflow to the approval and disclosure rules. It does not measure assessment speed, assessor workload or decision accuracy in live use, because no baseline review time or error rate exists; the benefits expected in the statement of need remain hypotheses for a later timed study. The test sets are small, so several comparisons may end inconclusive, and the report says so rather than claiming equivalence. Results on substitute data describe the methods on that data and do not predict results on sponsor submissions.")

